✅ Why people and not person?
Rails uses plural table names by default. It converts the model name Person (singular) to its plural form people using ActiveSupport::Inflector.

rails g model Person
Rails will:

Generate a model file:
app/models/person.rb

Generate a migration file (in db/migrate/) like:
XXXX_create_people.rb
(where XXXX is a timestamp)

Create a database table named people, not person.

